      "id": "finding-fc2198567b2419ae6a79633160d7173a3b6a7a9cd7c1807ea1aef9a8f49d7597",
      "ruleId": "built-in:code",
      "aspect": "correctness",
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "Optional grade is dereferenced without a guard",
      "description": "The header treats \u0060activeMeta().grade\u0060 as optional, but the summary card dereferences \u0060meta.grade.rationale\u0060, \u0060band\u0060, and \u0060score\u0060 whenever metadata exists. If metadata is available before its grade or legitimately lacks a grade, template evaluation will fail instead of rendering the existing fallback.",
      "recommendation": "Guard the summary card with \u0060@if (meta.grade; as grade)\u0060 and render a defined unavailable state otherwise, or make the data contract require a non-null grade and remove the contradictory optional access.",
