      "ruleId": "built-in:code",
      "aspect": "correctness",
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "Task status uses an identity that can be absent or collide",
      "description": "Finding selection and tracking explicitly fall back from \u0060fingerprint\u0060 to \u0060id\u0060, but task handover state is indexed only by \u0060finding.id\u0060. A fingerprint-only finding produces a shared \u0060kind:undefined\u0060 key, so unrelated findings can display or inherit the same creation status.",
      "recommendation": "Define one stable finding-key helper, such as \u0060findingKey(finding)\u0060, using the same fingerprint-or-id policy everywhere, and use it for selection, tracking, mutations, and handover status.",
